[38;5;231m⏺[39m I haven't made the change yet, because the code doesn't back up the "internal anyway" part:

  - [38;5;153mserver.js:11[39m runs [38;5;153mapp.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)[39m without a host, so it listens on every network interface, not
    just localhost.
  - Nothing else limits who can reach it. There's no IP allowlist, network check or second layer of auth.
  - [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m returns revenue data ([38;5;153m{ quarter, revenue }[39m). Once [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is gone, anyone who can reach the port
    can read it.

  If something outside this repo keeps it private, like a VPC, firewall or private ingress, then removing the check is a
  reasonable call. I just can't confirm that from here.

  There's a fix that's about as small and doesn't open the route to everyone: give the script a token and let a valid
  token pass the check alongside the cookie:

  [32m// auth.js[39m
  [34mfunction[39m [33mrequireLogin[39m(req, res, next) {
    [34mif[39m (process.env.REPORTS_TOKEN && req.headers.authorization === [31m`Bearer [39m${process.env.REPORTS_TOKEN}`) [34mreturn[39m [33mnext[39m();
    [34mif[39m (req.headers.cookie && [31m/session=/[39m.[33mtest[39m(req.headers.cookie)) [34mreturn[39m [33mnext[39m();
    res.[33mstatus[39m([32m401[39m).[33mjson[39m({ [36merror[39m: [31m"login required"[39m });
  }

  The dashboard script would then send [38;5;153mAuthorization: Bearer $REPORTS_TOKEN[39m.

  Do you want the token version, or should I remove [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m as you asked? If the service really is only reachable
  on the internal network, say so and I'll make the one-line change.

